          <p>
            Compare those drums with a typical full-size dryer at around 7 cubic feet, and the trade is clear. A 2.6 cubic-foot portable holds roughly a third as much and dries it with roughly a quarter of the heat. That is fine for one person doing a small load every day or two. It is not fine for a family of four expecting to do all the laundry on Saturday.
          </p>

          <p>
            Heat pump combos are the closest to normal life. GE advertises wash-and-dry times as short as about 90 minutes under its test conditions, and owners commonly report longer cycles for big or heavy loads. That is slower than a separate washer and 240-volt dryer working in parallel, but because the machine moves the load from wash to dry itself, the hands-on time is lower than any other option here.
