        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            If you have a water hookup and drain but no vent or 240-volt outlet, buy a heat pump combo: the GE Profile UltraFast Combo for most people, the LG WashCombo if you want the biggest drum. If you already have a washer, the Miele T1 TXD160WP is the best standalone 120-volt dryer we found, and GE's 24-inch combo is the answer for the tightest spaces.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            If the budget is closer to $300 and your laundry volume is small, a vented portable from Panda, BLACK+DECKER or Magic Chef will do the job, as long as you vent it outside, keep loads moderate and give it a circuit of its own. Expect slower cycles than a full-size dryer, plan around them, and you will still beat a trip to the laundromat.
          </p>
